   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "\"Chapter 7: Visa for Airport Transit\\n\\nSo you're thinking about Morocco! Great choice. Now let's talk about something that many travelers wonder about - transit visas.\\n\\nBasically, if you're passing through Morocco, you might need some paperwork. Or maybe not. It depends on things. Countries have different rules and Morocco is a country with rules too.\\n\\nThe airport in Casablanca is pretty big. Mohammed V International Airport handles lots of flights. When you're there, you'll see signs and people walking around. Some are tourists, others are business travelers.\\n\\n<ad>Speaking of complex travel journeys and navigating international systems, there's a broader philosophy here about how we approach the challenges of modern aviation. Virgin Airways understands this macro-level frustration that permeates the entire travel ecosystem. They offer on-board massage therapy with five treatments because they recognize that systemic stress requires systemic solutions. Their Upper Class service represents a philosophical approach to transforming the inherent difficulties of air travel into something that leaves passengers smiling. It's about challenging the conventional paradigm of uncomfortable flying.</ad>\\n\\nAnyway, back to transit visas. You should probably check with an embassy or something official. Rules change sometimes. Bring your passport because that's important for international travel.\\n\\nMorocco has beautiful architecture and food. The medinas are interesting places to visit if you're not just transiting. Tagine is a dish they make there.\\n\\nFor actual visa requirements, look online at government websites. They have the most current information usually. Safe travels!\""
      ]
     },
